@startuml 08-state-runtime
' pnt-edge: Runtime lifecycle driven by the main loop (SAD section 6.4)
title Runtime lifecycle and the recovery ladder
[*] --> Starting : main(): config, Hub, Updater, WebServer
Starting --> Running : start_runtime()\nfilter + input + output built, input started
Running --> Rebuilding : solution watchdog\n(no solution for solution_watchdog_s\nwhile measurements arrive)
Running --> Rebuilding : host clock step\nand input uses host clock
Running --> Rebuilding : reset filter\n($PPNT or web)
Running --> Rebuilding : set_nmea / save_config\n(NMEA block changed)
Running --> Rebuilding : looped log ended
Rebuilding --> Running : stop_runtime(), start_runtime()
Running --> Stopping : SIGINT / SIGTERM
Running --> Stopping : reset app\n(web, $PPNT, update applied)
Stopping --> [*] : exit code (filter stop)
Stopping --> ReExec : g_exit_code == 3
ReExec --> Starting : execv(exe_path) succeeds\n(new image, same pid)
ReExec --> [*] : execv fails -> exit 3
note bottom
  Outer rungs, outside this process:
  systemd Restart=always RestartSec=2 (exists)
  systemd WatchdogSec via sd_notify (planned)
  Tegra hardware watchdog, A/B rootfs (Phase C)
end note
@enduml
